WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.170
An MRI scanner builds pictures
of the inside of your body.

2
00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:09.610
It does it by detecting hydrogen
nuclei, held in a strong magnetic field.

3
00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:14.590
Chemists use the same effect on a
single compound, in a narrow glass tube.

4
00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:18.130
So what can the same effect
tell a chemist about a molecule?

5
00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:21.910
In this mission, you'll
read proton NMR spectra:

6
00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:26.690
where each signal sits, the area
beneath it, and how it splits.

7
00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:30.510
You'll work through ethanol's
spectrum, first at low resolution,

8
00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:34.450
then at high resolution,
using the n + 1 rule.

9
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:39.160
Your mission: find out what an NMR
spectrum reveals about a molecule.
